Morocco has stepped up security along its borders with the Spanish enclaves of Ceuta and Melilla after fresh calls appeared on social media urging migrants to attempt another mass crossing, weeks after tens of thousands rushed the frontier.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3276abb4-96ef-11f1-a5ad-b3954165afe0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:59:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Romania shuts down nuclear plant due to low level of drought-hit Danube</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260813-romania-shuts-down-nuclear-plant-due-to-low-level-of-drought-hit-danube</link><description>
Romania on Thursday began a complete shutdown of its only nuclear plant after levels of water in the River Danube – used to cool the site – fell to a record low, the national nuclear energy company said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ed108bc2-96fc-11f1-89c1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26219541763429.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ed108bc2-96fc-11f1-89c1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26219541763429.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7fa3daf8-96fc-11f1-b324-8fa549d9c748</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:28:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ed108bc2-96fc-11f1-89c1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26219541763429.jpg">AP Photo/Andreea Alexandru - Andreea Alexandru</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Voters in Zambia to deliver verdict on president's economic record</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260813-voters-in-zambia-to-deliver-verdict-on-president-s-economic-record</link><description>
Zambia are voting in a general election on Thursday which will decide whether President Hakainde Hichilema returns for a second term, after steering the country out of a debt crisis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c3327da-7c10-11f1-b608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T081147Z-165481622-RC243MA7WI20-RTRMADP-3-ZAMBIA-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c3327da-7c10-11f1-b608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T081147Z-165481622-RC243MA7WI20-RTRMADP-3-ZAMBIA-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">adbb8c54-9640-11f1-af52-33e74b5f3d09</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:01:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8c3327da-7c10-11f1-b608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T081147Z-165481622-RC243MA7WI20-RTRMADP-3-ZAMBIA-ELECTION.jpg">© REUTERS - MOSES MWAPE </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>French ambassador to CAR disciplined over misconduct allegations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260812-french-ambassador-to-car-disciplined-over-misconduct-allegations</link><description>
France’s foreign ministry has launched disciplinary proceedings against its ambassador to the Central African Republic, following allegations that he repeatedly brought young women to the official residence in Bangui and had sexual relations with some of them.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38edf5ea-9624-11f1-aab5-b1eab2020edd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:02:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/051412da-9634-11f1-8957-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/french-ambassador-bangui.jpeg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Can UK's hard-right Farage bin financial probe with by-election win?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-can-uk-s-hard-right-farage-bin-financial-probe-with-snap-poll</link><description>
Nigel Farage – leader of the anti-immigration Reform UK party – will be fighting for his parliamentary seat on Thursday, going head to head with parody candidate Count Binface in snap polls. The by-election was called after Farage resigned amid a probe into his finances. But the surprise move threatens to backfire as none of the major political parties has fielded a candidate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7d7d4b0-9635-11f1-a27e-35fc75775395</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:38:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg">© Jon Super / AP Photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Millions gather to watch as solar eclipse plunges swathe of Spain into darkness</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260813-as-millions-gazed-in-awe-a-swathe-of-spain-plunged-into-darkness</link><description>
Millions of spectators – tourists and locals alike – gathered in parks and cities across Spain to see Wednesday's total solar eclipse, the first of its kind in the country in more than a century.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5567e238-96df-11f1-8aa3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Observator-astrofizic-Arcos-de-las-Salinas-Spania.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5567e238-96df-11f1-8aa3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Observator-astrofizic-Arcos-de-las-Salinas-Spania.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">439102cc-96e1-11f1-8094-3395aad33fd5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 06:39:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5567e238-96df-11f1-8aa3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Observator-astrofizic-Arcos-de-las-Salinas-Spania.jpg">© REUTERS - Christian Hartmann</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran faces growing isolation and uncertain future amid 'dire' economic situation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-iran-faces-growing-isolation-and-uncertain-future-amid-dire-economic-situation</link><description>
As economic pressure mounts in Iran, RFI spoke to economist Djamchid Assadi about how this is leaving the country more isolated and strengthening the role of the Revolutionary Guards.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94c5695e-9627-11f1-8ead-1f957f32f043</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 18:48:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg">AP Photo/Vahid Salemi - Vahid Salemi</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Russia threatens retaliatory seizures of EU ships amid new sanctions push</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-russia-threatens-retaliatory-seizures-of-eu-ships-amid-new-sanctions-push</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday threatened to seize ships belonging to European countries in retaliation for plans to sell off cargo seized from Russian "shadow fleet" vessels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e58d70ac-964a-11f1-b3ed-8940524ed401</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:52:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg">© Ints Kalnins / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France gripped by latest summer heatwave as drought conditions worsen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260812-france-gripped-by-latest-summer-heatwave-as-drought-conditions-worsen</link><description>
Scorching heat continued to spread across most of mainland France on Wednesday, as the Ministry for Ecological Transition met to take stock of the effects of a drought that has been steadily worsening since May. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee532400-9624-11f1-9288-8fc7ca80b067</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:38:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg">REUTERS - Stephane Mahe</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Hungary elects Orban critic Andras Baka as first president in new political era</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-hungary-elects-orban-critic-andras-baka-as-first-president-of-new-political-era</link><description>
Hungarian lawmakers on Tuesday approved former supreme court chief Andras Baka – a prominent critic of Viktor Orban who was ousted during the ex-premier's time in power – as the country's next head of state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762bbf5c-9613-11f1-a50c-03e5429215e8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:36:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg">Szilard Koszticsak/MTI via AP - Szilard Koszticsak</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Assisted dying, social media and agriculture put France’s top court in spotlight</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-assisted-dying-social-media-and-agriculture-put-france-s-top-court-in-spotlight</link><description>
France’s Constitutional Council is facing a politically charged end to the summer, with judges due to rule on a series of high-profile laws – including those covering assisted dying, social media use by children, agriculture and public security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">794857bc-956f-11f1-8018-6bca3bd6865c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:01:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg">© Christophe BONNET</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Lebanon becomes first country in Middle East to abolish death penalty</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-lebanon-becomes-first-country-in-middle-east-to-abolish-death-penalty</link><description>
Lebanon’s parliament on Tuesday abolished the death penalty, making it the first country in the Middle East to replace capital punishment with a sentence of life imprisonment with hard labour. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b65aa9ac-957e-11f1-844e-7385b0464f2f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:14:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG">REUTERS/Mohamed Azakir</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Former Syrian leader Assad sentenced to death in absentia over war crimes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-former-syrian-leader-assad-sentenced-to-death-in-absentia-over-war-crimes</link><description>
A Syrian court on Tuesday sentenced former ruler Bashar al-Assad to death after a trial in absentia, convicting him of atrocities committed during the country's civil war. Six of his closest aides were also handed death sentences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73c8abca-956f-11f1-aff4-e70fbbb452ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:58:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg">AFP - LOUAI BESHARA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Race to find Ebola vaccine as DR Congo outbreak kills more than 2,000</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260812-race-to-find-ebola-vaccine-as-dr-congo-outbreak-kills-more-than-2-000</link><description>
The latest outbreak of Ebola has killed more than 2,000 people in the Democratic Republic of Congo, according to health authorities. Meanwhile, international efforts have been stepped up to test a vaccine for the highly contagious haemorrhagic fever.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7534c1c2-962f-11f1-b43d-f3a546cf71d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:44:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg">AP Photo/Dieudonne Dirole - Dieudonne Dirole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and EU join international aid effort after Colombia earthquake</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-france-eu-join-international-aid-effort-after-colombia-earthquake</link><description>
France has joined the European Union and a host of countries in offering assistance to Colombia, where volunteers and rescuers are searching for survivors following Monday's deadly earthquake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e96a684-955e-11f1-bebd-75c492606bc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:08:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg">© Jamie Saldarriaga / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>May ’68 protest leader Cohn-Bendit pledges support to Glucksmann for 2027</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260810-may-68-veteran-cohn-bendit-throws-support-behind-left-wing-glucksmann-for-2027</link><description>
Former Green MEP Daniel Cohn-Bendit, a historic figure on the French left, on Monday gave his support to Raphaël Glucksmann for France’s 2027 presidential election, in an interview with Le Point magazine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a90b0ffe-94b5-11f1-ba5c-c57808d5257e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:00:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebel forces in Ethiopia's Tigray state condemn army drone strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260811-rebel-forces-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-state-condemn-army-drone-strikes</link><description>
Rebel authorities on Tuesday accused the Ethiopian government of carrying out deadly drone strikes in southern Tigray state and condemned the move as "a serious escalation", amid fears of a new war. 
